## Why <%= importPath %>?

- **One call composes it** — `<%= alias %>()` registers this package's capabilities with `defineRuntime`.
- **Role factories** — <% for (const [index, capability] of capabilities.entries()) { %><%= index > 0 ? ', ' : '' %>`<%= capability.factoryName %>()`<% } %> support direct authoring, isolated tests, and whole-role ordering outside plugin expansion.
- **No module-scope work** — backends load in `initialize()` and stay in capability context, one payload per worker.

## Install

```bash
npm i <%= importPath %> @taucad/runtime
```

`@taucad/runtime` is a required peer — one install must hold one runtime. A capability with an
options schema adds `zod` as a second required peer.

## Quick start

```typescript
import { defineRuntime } from '@taucad/runtime/worker';
import { <%= alias %> } from '<%= importPath %>';

const runtime = defineRuntime({ plugins: [<%= alias %>()] });
```

Hand the definition to a client — `createNodeClient`, `createRuntimeWorker`, or your own host. See
[`@taucad/runtime`](https://www.npmjs.com/package/@taucad/runtime) for the client lifecycle.

## API

| Export | Kind | Use |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `<%= alias %>` | toolkit factory | package-named authoring factory; presets select capabilities |
| `plugin` | toolkit factory | the same factory under its mechanical name, for loaders that read a fixed key |
<% for (const capability of capabilities) { %>| `<%= capability.factoryName %>` | <%= capability.role %> factory | direct `<%= capability.bucket %>` composition, with options |
<% } %>
One preset, `default`, selecting <% for (const [index, capability] of capabilities.entries()) { %><%= index > 0 ? ', ' : '' %>`<%= capability.bucket %>.default`<% } %>.

